      "answer": "In Gloomhaven (2nd Edition), **advantage** works with attack modifier cards as follows:\n\n> With **advantage**, the attacker draws two modifiers and uses one of them. A monster always uses the better one, but a character may use either one.\n\n**With rolling modifiers:** If the first draw is a rolling modifier, you continue drawing additional modifiers one at a time until you get a non-rolling modifier, then draw one more. You then use all the initial rolling modifiers plus whichever of the final two non-rolling modifiers you choose (or the better one, if you're a monster).\n\n**Special cases:**\n- If the first draw is *not* a rolling modifier but the second draw is, the rolling icon on the second modifier is still ignored.\n- An attack cannot have both advantage and disadvantage; if it does, it has neither.\n- **Any ranged attack on an adjacent enemy automatically gains disadvantage** (not advantage).",
